# The generated SDK IS committed, deliberately.
#
# It was gitignored at first, which left this repo with six config files and no SDK: a
# clone was not browsable, not installable from a git URL, and required Docker to see
# anything at all. That is wrong for a client library, whatever its merits for a private
# prototype.
#
# Committing it is what Anthropic's and Stainless's SDK repos do, and it buys the thing
# that matters most during review: a spec change produces a readable diff showing what
# happened to the PUBLIC API. "This renamed a method" is exactly the change that is
# expensive to discover after publishing.
#
# So sdks/ is tracked. Regenerate with:
#   fern generate --local
# and commit the result as its own commit, so the machine-written diff stays separate from
# hand-written changes.

# Fern working files
**/.preview
**/.definition

# Dependencies and build output inside the generated tree: reproducible from source, and
# node_modules in particular would be tens of thousands of files.
node_modules/
sdks/typescript/node_modules/
sdks/typescript/dist/
sdks/typescript/package-lock.json
